# admintool / eip

Canonical docs (follow these):
- [docs/admintool/TUI.md](../../docs/admintool/TUI.md)
- [docs/admintool/VARIABLES.md](../../docs/admintool/VARIABLES.md)
- [docs/admintool/ENGINEERING.md](../../docs/admintool/ENGINEERING.md)

## SoT — no hardcoding

- Reused strings/lists have **one** source of truth (see VARIABLES.md).
- CLI verbs: `internal/catalog`. Home TUI menu titles / helpers / gating: `tui/ops` (`Entries` / `MoreEntries` / `SetupNeeded`) — plain-language; `Args` keep CLI ids. Do not paste parallel menu tables in screens.
- Product name/tagline: `internal/kit` only.
- Theme/gutters: `tui/theme` only.
- Env keys: `kit/templates/env.EnvFields()`; YAML defaults: `yamldefaults.DefaultConfig()`; YAML edit knobs: `yamldefaults.ConfigFields()` — stay under templates. Live YAML load/sync: `internal/config`. Do not invent parallel key lists in the UI.
- **Process** SoT: `internal/process` (`EIP_FROM_TUI` / `FromTUI`, `ChildEnv`, `HoldOnError`) ≠ **`.env` keys**. Prefix `eip`/`EIP_` for OS-facing names (incl. `EIPMSG ` wire); packages/types unprefixed (`msg`, `chip.docker`). See VARIABLES.md.

## Helpers — no duplication

- Extract helpers for repeated actions (panels, lists, `exec.Run`, file IO).
- New UI chrome goes in `tui/ui` / `tui/theme`, not copy-pasted into screens.

## Folder hygiene

- Full-screen flows → `tui/screens/<name>/`.
- Update docs package maps when structure changes.
- **No `doc.go` note files** — write `docs/admintool/` instead.

## Docker — SDK first

- Use **Docker Go SDK** via `internal/docker.NewClient` / `Probe` (`ResolveDockerEndpoint` for CLI context Host). Do **not** use bare `FromEnv` alone, inspect OS services, or raw Engine HTTP when the SDK can do it.
- **TUI:** never Docker in-process — shell `eip <verb>`; verbs use the SDK.
- **No SDK coverage?** Stop and **flag before implementing** an API workaround; explain the gap. Prefer wrapping the SDK if a cleaner approach exists.
- Details: [docs/admintool/ENGINEERING.md](../../docs/admintool/ENGINEERING.md) § Docker access.

## TUI runtime

- **TUI-first:** no-args / double-click → TUI. Existing shell → TUI in that window, quit returns to prompt. No success-path console pause or CLI sermon.
- Child-process ops only (`tui/exec`, `EIP_FROM_TUI=1`); never Cobra/Docker in-process.
- Chip updates via `EIPMSG` `chip.*` / `internal/msg` → `Snapshot`; menu gates on `snap.Docker`.
- OUTPUT pane via `EIPMSG` `pane.*` / `internal/msg` + stderr errors → `tui/pane.Buffer` (append + follow). Per-command formatters in `tui/output/<verb>/`. Non-protocol stdout discarded under TUI. Background `eip probe` never emits `pane.*`.
- Keyboard-only (swallow `MouseMsg`); TUI styles ≠ Cobra.
- **Build lock:** use `.\scripts\admintool\build-host.ps1` (or `.sh`) → repo-root `eip.exe` / `eip` only (**no `dist/`**). If locked: **ALERT**, stop running `eip` processes, retry. **Never** write alternate names (`eip-tui9.exe`, etc.).
- Config SoT remains `.env` + `eip.config.yaml`. Setup / Secrets / Settings persist via `screens/home/docs.go` + `screens/init`; day-2 Persist may auto-queue child `secrets`/`sync` (no Apply menu rows).
- Menu shape: Main (Setup if docs missing · Status · Start · Dev · Restart · Rebuild · Stop · Update · More); More (Secrets · Settings · Logs · Command). Children opened from More return to More.
